#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "IBM Quantum Composer is a graphical programming tool. Drag and drop operations to build circuits and run them on quantum hardware."
msgstr "IBM Quantum Composer adalah alat pemrograman grafis. Seret dan lepas operasi untuk membangun Circuit dan menjalankannya di perangkat keras kuantum."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "IBM Quantum Composer"
msgstr "IBM Quantum Composer"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* cspell:ignore gatename, ungroup, ungrouping */}\n"
msgstr "{/* cspell:ignore gatename, ungroup, ungrouping */}\n"

#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "IBM Quantum Composer {#ibm-quantum-composer}"
msgstr "IBM Quantum Composer {#ibm-quantum-composer}"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "What is it? {#what-is-it}"
msgstr "Apa itu IBM Quantum Composer? {#what-is-it}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[IBM Quantum&reg; Composer](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/composer) is a graphical quantum programming tool that lets you drag and drop operations to build quantum circuits and run them on quantum hardware.\n"
msgstr "[IBM Quantum&reg; Composer](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/composer) adalah alat pemrograman kuantum berbasis grafis yang memungkinkan kamu menyeret dan melepas operasi untuk membangun Circuit kuantum dan menjalankannya di perangkat keras kuantum.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "What can it do? {#what-can-it-do}"
msgstr "Apa yang bisa dilakukan? {#what-can-it-do}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Visualize qubit states**\n"
msgstr "**Visualisasikan status qubit**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "See how changes to your circuit affect the state of qubits, shown as an interactive q-sphere, or histograms showing measurement probabilities or statevector simulations.\n"
msgstr "Lihat bagaimana perubahan pada Circuit-mu memengaruhi status qubit, yang ditampilkan sebagai q-sphere interaktif, atau histogram yang menunjukkan probabilitas pengukuran atau simulasi statevector.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Run on quantum hardware**\n"
msgstr "**Jalankan di perangkat keras kuantum**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run your circuits on real quantum hardware to understand the effects of device noise.\n"
msgstr "Jalankan Circuit-mu di perangkat keras kuantum nyata untuk memahami efek noise dari perangkat.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Automatically generate code**\n"
msgstr "**Buat kode secara otomatis**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instead of writing code by hand, automatically generate OpenQASM or Python code that behaves the same way as the circuit you created with the Composer.\n"
msgstr "Daripada menulis kode secara manual, buat kode OpenQASM atau Python secara otomatis yang berperilaku sama seperti Circuit yang kamu buat dengan Composer.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tour of the interface {#tour-of-the-interface}"
msgstr "Tur antarmuka {#tour-of-the-interface}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "IBM Quantum Composer has a customizable set of tools that allow you to build, visualize, and run quantum circuits on quantum processing units (QPUs). Use the \"More options\" menu on each window to access additional tools and actions.\n"
msgstr "IBM Quantum Composer memiliki sekumpulan alat yang dapat dikustomisasi untuk membangun, memvisualisasikan, dan menjalankan Circuit kuantum di unit pemrosesan kuantum (QPU). Gunakan menu \"More options\" di setiap jendela untuk mengakses alat dan tindakan tambahan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![IBM Quantum Composer window](/docs/images/guides/composer/composer-annotation.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Jendela IBM Quantum Composer.](/docs/images/guides/composer/composer-annotation.svg)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Operations catalog** - These are the building blocks of quantum circuits. Drag and drop these gates and other operations onto the graphical circuit editor. Different types of gates are grouped together by color. For example, classical gates are dark blue, phase gates are light blue, and non-unitary operations are grey.\n"
msgstr "**Katalog operasi** - Ini adalah blok pembangun Circuit kuantum. Seret dan lepas Gate dan operasi lainnya ke editor Circuit grafis. Berbagai jenis Gate dikelompokkan berdasarkan warna. Misalnya, Gate klasik berwarna biru tua, Gate fase berwarna biru muda, dan operasi non-unitary berwarna abu-abu.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   To learn about the available gates and operations, right-click an operation and select Info to read its definition.\n"
msgstr "   Untuk mempelajari Gate dan operasi yang tersedia, klik kanan suatu operasi dan pilih Info untuk membaca definisinya.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Code editor** - Use the View menu to open or close the code editor, which allows you to view the OpenQASM or Qiskit code for the circuit. You can edit the OpenQASM code; the Qiskit code is read-only.\n"
msgstr "**Editor kode** - Gunakan menu View untuk membuka atau menutup editor kode, yang memungkinkan kamu melihat kode OpenQASM atau Qiskit untuk Circuit. Kamu bisa mengedit kode OpenQASM; kode Qiskit bersifat read-only.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Graphical circuit editor** - This is where you build a circuit. Drag gates and other operations onto the horizontal qubit “wires” that make up your quantum register.\n"
msgstr "**Editor Circuit grafis** - Di sinilah kamu membangun Circuit. Seret Gate dan operasi lainnya ke \"kabel\" Qubit horizontal yang membentuk register kuantum-mu.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   To remove a gate from a wire, select the gate and click the trash can icon.\n"
msgstr "   Untuk menghapus Gate dari kabel, pilih Gate tersebut dan klik ikon tempat sampah.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   To edit the parameters and settings on gates that support editing, select the gate on the graphical editor and click Edit.\n"
msgstr "   Untuk mengedit parameter dan pengaturan pada Gate yang mendukung pengeditan, pilih Gate di editor grafis dan klik Edit.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Toolbar** - Access frequently used tools to undo and redo actions, change the gate alignment, and switch to inspect mode. With inspect mode, you see a step-by-step view of the qubit states as you circuit computation evolves. To learn more, see [Inspect your circuit, step-by-step](#4-inspect-your-circuit-step-by-step).\n"
msgstr "**Toolbar** - Akses alat yang sering digunakan untuk membatalkan dan mengulang tindakan, mengubah perataan Gate, dan beralih ke mode inspeksi. Dengan mode inspeksi, kamu bisa melihat tampilan langkah demi langkah dari status qubit saat komputasi Circuit-mu berkembang. Untuk mempelajari lebih lanjut, lihat [Periksa Circuit-mu, langkah demi langkah](#4-inspect-your-circuit-step-by-step).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Phase disks** - The phase of the qubit state vector in the complex plane is given by the line that extends from the center of the diagram to the edge of the gray disk (which rotates counterclockwise around the center point).\n"
msgstr "**Cakram fase** - Fase vektor status qubit di bidang kompleks ditunjukkan oleh garis yang memanjang dari pusat diagram ke tepi cakram abu-abu (yang berputar berlawanan arah jarum jam di sekitar titik pusat).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "    Use the View menu to show or hide the phase disks.\n"
msgstr "    Gunakan menu View untuk menampilkan atau menyembunyikan cakram fase.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '6. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Visualizations** - Visualizations characterize your circuit as you build it. They use a single-shot statevector simulator, which is different from the QPU specified in the \"Run circuit\" settings. Note that the visualizations ignore any measurement operations you add. Sign in and click **Run circuit** to get results from the specified backend instead.\n"
msgstr "**Visualisasi** - Visualisasi mencirikan Circuit-mu saat kamu membangunnya. Visualisasi menggunakan simulator statevector single-shot, yang berbeda dari QPU yang ditentukan dalam pengaturan \"Run circuit\". Perlu diperhatikan bahwa visualisasi mengabaikan operasi pengukuran apa pun yang kamu tambahkan. Masuk dan klik **Run circuit** untuk mendapatkan hasil dari Backend yang ditentukan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   Learn more in the [Visualizations](#visualizations) section.\n"
msgstr "   Pelajari lebih lanjut di bagian [Visualisasi](#visualizations).\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build, edit, and inspect quantum circuits {#build-edit-and-inspect-quantum-circuits}"
msgstr "Bangun, edit, dan periksa Circuit kuantum {#build-edit-and-inspect-quantum-circuits}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<Admonition type=\"warning\" title=\"Download your circuit files before exiting the Composer\">\n"
msgstr "<Admonition type=\"warning\" title=\"Unduh file Circuit-mu sebelum keluar dari Composer\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you want to continue working with a circuit at a later time, be sure to download your circuit file and store it locally before exiting your current Composer session. Use the \"Save file\" link in the upper-right corner, or go to the File menu and choose \"Save file\". When you are ready to work with the circuit again, go to the File menu and choose \"Upload .qasm file\", then navigate to your circuit file on your local drive and click Open.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika kamu ingin melanjutkan mengerjakan Circuit di lain waktu, pastikan untuk mengunduh file Circuit-mu dan menyimpannya secara lokal sebelum keluar dari sesi Composer yang sedang berjalan. Gunakan tautan \"Save file\" di pojok kanan atas, atau buka menu File dan pilih \"Save file\". Saat kamu siap untuk mengerjakan Circuit kembali, buka menu File dan pilih \"Upload .qasm file\", lalu navigasi ke file Circuit-mu di drive lokal dan klik Open.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. Open IBM Quantum Composer {#1-open-ibm-quantum-composer}"
msgstr "1. Buka IBM Quantum Composer {#1-open-ibm-quantum-composer}"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "(Optional) If you are not currently signed in to IBM Quantum, select **Sign in** in the upper right corner. Then, you can either sign in or **Create an IBM Cloud account**.\n"
msgstr "(Opsional) Jika kamu belum masuk ke IBM Quantum, pilih **Sign in** di pojok kanan atas. Kemudian, kamu bisa masuk atau **Create an IBM Cloud account**.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"   If you don’t sign in, the visualizations automatically show simulated results for up to four qubits. If you want to run your circuit on a quantum computer, or if you want to visualize a circuit that has more than four qubits, you must sign in.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"   Jika kamu tidak masuk, visualisasi akan secara otomatis menampilkan hasil simulasi untuk hingga empat qubit. Jika kamu ingin menjalankan Circuit di komputer kuantum, atau jika kamu ingin memvisualisasikan Circuit yang memiliki lebih dari empat qubit, kamu harus masuk.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Open IBM Quantum Composer by clicking the link on the [Learning page](/learning) navigation. The workspace displays an untitled empty circuit. You can either create a new circuit, or upload a .qasm file to continue working with with a circuit you've already created. \n"
msgstr "Buka IBM Quantum Composer dengan mengklik tautan di navigasi [halaman Learning](/learning). Workspace menampilkan Circuit kosong tanpa judul. Kamu bisa membuat Circuit baru, atau mengunggah file .qasm untuk melanjutkan mengerjakan Circuit yang sudah pernah kamu buat.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Name your circuit by clicking on the words **Untitled circuit** and typing in a name for your circuit. Click the checkmark to save the name.\n"
msgstr "Beri nama Circuit-mu dengan mengklik kata **Untitled circuit** dan ketik nama untuk Circuit-mu. Klik tanda centang untuk menyimpan nama tersebut.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "(Optional) Customize your workspace:\n"
msgstr "(Opsional) Kustomisasi workspace-mu:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '   * '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use the **View** menu to change from the default theme to a monochrome theme. You can also select which panels to include on your workspace, then use the menu in the right corner of any panel to access options for further customization. The options to show or hide phase disks, choose the alignment of the qubits on your circuit, and reset the workspace to the default are in the View menu as well.\n"
msgstr "Gunakan menu **View** untuk beralih dari tema default ke tema monokrom. Kamu juga bisa memilih panel mana yang ingin disertakan di workspace-mu, lalu gunakan menu di pojok kanan panel mana pun untuk mengakses opsi kustomisasi lebih lanjut. Opsi untuk menampilkan atau menyembunyikan cakram fase, memilih perataan qubit di Circuit-mu, dan mengatur ulang workspace ke default juga ada di menu View.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '   * '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Switch between dark and light workspace themes in the bottom-right corner of the footer.\n"
msgstr "Beralih antara tema workspace gelap dan terang di pojok kanan bawah footer.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To build a circuit, you can either [drag and drop operations](#2-build-your-circuit-with-drag-and-drop), or you can enter [OpenQASM code](#3-build-your-circuit-with-openqasm-code) into the code editor.\n"
msgstr "Untuk membangun Circuit, kamu bisa [menyeret dan melepas operasi](#2-build-your-circuit-with-drag-and-drop), atau memasukkan [kode OpenQASM](#3-build-your-circuit-with-openqasm-code) ke editor kode.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Build your circuit with drag-and-drop {#2-build-your-circuit-with-drag-and-drop}"
msgstr "2. Bangun Circuit-mu dengan drag-and-drop {#2-build-your-circuit-with-drag-and-drop}"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Operations catalog {#operations-catalog}"
msgstr "Katalog operasi {#operations-catalog}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Drag and drop operations from the operations catalog onto the quantum and classical registers. Click the search icon and enter a term in the search bar to quickly find an operation.\n"
msgstr "Seret dan lepas operasi dari katalog operasi ke register kuantum dan klasik. Klik ikon pencarian dan masukkan istilah di kotak pencarian untuk menemukan operasi dengan cepat.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Collapse and expand the operations catalog by clicking the icon in the upper right corner of the operations panel. Click the icon next to it to toggle between a grid and list view of the catalog.\n"
msgstr "Perkecil dan perbesar katalog operasi dengan mengklik ikon di pojok kanan atas panel operasi. Klik ikon di sebelahnya untuk beralih antara tampilan grid dan list dari katalog.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Right-click an operation icon and select Info to view the definition of an operation, along with its QASM reference.\n"
msgstr "Klik kanan ikon operasi dan pilih Info untuk melihat definisi suatu operasi, beserta referensi QASM-nya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To undo or redo, use the curved arrows in the toolbar.\n"
msgstr "Untuk membatalkan atau mengulang, gunakan panah melengkung di toolbar.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Alignment {#alignment}"
msgstr "Perataan {#alignment}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choose Freeform alignment to place operations anywhere on the circuit. For a more compact view of your circuit, choose Left alignment. To see the order in which operations will execute, choose Layers alignment, which will apply left alignment and add column delineators that indicate the execution order, from left to right and top to bottom.\n"
msgstr "Pilih perataan Freeform untuk menempatkan operasi di mana saja di Circuit. Untuk tampilan Circuit yang lebih ringkas, pilih perataan Left. Untuk melihat urutan eksekusi operasi, pilih perataan Layers, yang akan menerapkan perataan kiri dan menambahkan pemisah kolom yang menunjukkan urutan eksekusi, dari kiri ke kanan dan atas ke bawah.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Once operations are placed on your circuit, you can continue to drag and drop them to new positions.\n"
msgstr "Setelah operasi ditempatkan di Circuit-mu, kamu tetap bisa menyeret dan melepasnya ke posisi baru.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Copy and paste {#copy-and-paste}"
msgstr "Salin dan tempel {#copy-and-paste}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Click an operation and use the icons in the contextual menu to copy and paste it.\n"
msgstr "Klik suatu operasi dan gunakan ikon di menu kontekstual untuk menyalin dan menempelkannya.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Select multiple operations {#select-multiple-operations}"
msgstr "Pilih beberapa operasi {#select-multiple-operations}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can select several operations to copy and paste them, drag them to a new location, or group them into a custom unitary operation that displays in your operations catalog and functions as a single gate.\n"
msgstr "Kamu bisa memilih beberapa operasi untuk menyalin dan menempelkannya, menyeretnya ke lokasi baru, atau mengelompokkannya menjadi operasi unitary kustom yang tampil di katalog operasi-mu dan berfungsi sebagai satu Gate tunggal.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To select more than one operation, place your cursor just outside one of the operations, then click and drag across the area to select. Shift-click individual operations to select or deselect them. A dashed line outlines the set of operations you are selecting, and each operation that is actually part of the selection is outlined in blue.\n"
msgstr "Untuk memilih lebih dari satu operasi, tempatkan kursor tepat di luar salah satu operasi, lalu klik dan seret melintasi area tersebut untuk memilih. Shift-klik operasi individual untuk memilih atau membatalkan pilihan. Garis putus-putus akan menggaris bawahi kumpulan operasi yang sedang kamu pilih, dan setiap operasi yang benar-benar merupakan bagian dari pilihan akan dilingkari dengan biru.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For example, in the following image, the Hadamard gate on q1 and the CX gate are selected. The Hadamard gate on q0 is not selected.\n"
msgstr "Misalnya, pada gambar berikut, Gate Hadamard di q1 dan Gate CX dipilih. Gate Hadamard di q0 tidak dipilih.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A set of selected operations](/docs/images/guides/composer/3c5c063d-b15f-43cb-bb65-9728187454d8.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Sekumpulan operasi yang dipilih.](/docs/images/guides/composer/3c5c063d-b15f-43cb-bb65-9728187454d8.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Select Copy from the contextual menu to copy the group.\n"
msgstr "Pilih Copy dari menu kontekstual untuk menyalin grup tersebut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To paste the group of operations, right-click in the circuit and select Paste.\n"
msgstr "Untuk menempel grup operasi, klik kanan di Circuit dan pilih Paste.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build a custom operation using the group feature {#build-a-custom-operation-using-the-group-feature}"
msgstr "Bangun operasi kustom menggunakan fitur group {#build-a-custom-operation-using-the-group-feature}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To group several operations together and save them as a custom operation, first select the operations as described above, then select Group from the contextual menu. You are prompted to name the custom operation or you can accept the default name. Click OK, and the custom operation will be represented by a single box, both in your circuit and in the operations catalog.\n"
msgstr "Untuk mengelompokkan beberapa operasi bersama dan menyimpannya sebagai operasi kustom, pertama pilih operasi seperti yang dijelaskan di atas, lalu pilih Group dari menu kontekstual. Kamu akan diminta untuk memberi nama operasi kustom tersebut atau bisa menerima nama default. Klik OK, dan operasi kustom akan direpresentasikan sebagai satu kotak, baik di Circuit-mu maupun di katalog operasi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can now drag and drop the new operation throughout your circuit. Note that the operation is saved to this circuit but does not appear in the operations catalog for other circuits.\n"
msgstr "Kamu sekarang bisa menyeret dan melepas operasi baru tersebut ke seluruh bagian Circuit-mu. Perlu diperhatikan bahwa operasi tersebut tersimpan di Circuit ini dan tidak muncul di katalog operasi untuk Circuit lain.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can also build a custom operation directly in the OpenQASM code editor; see [Create a custom operation in OpenQASM](#create-a-custom-operation-in-openqasm) for more information.\n"
msgstr "Kamu juga bisa membangun operasi kustom langsung di editor kode OpenQASM; lihat [Buat operasi kustom di OpenQASM](#create-a-custom-operation-in-openqasm) untuk informasi lebih lanjut.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Ungroup a custom or predefined operation {#ungroup-a-custom-or-predefined-operation}"
msgstr "Ungroup operasi kustom atau predefined {#ungroup-a-custom-or-predefined-operation}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To ungroup the gates within a custom or predefined operation, click the operation on the Composer and select Ungroup from the contextual menu. You can now move the separate operations individually. When you ungroup an operation, each element in the former group executes independently, which may mean they execute in a different order from when they were grouped together.\n"
msgstr "Untuk memisahkan Gate dalam operasi kustom atau predefined, klik operasi di Composer dan pilih Ungroup dari menu kontekstual. Kamu sekarang bisa memindahkan operasi yang terpisah secara individual. Saat kamu ungroup suatu operasi, setiap elemen dalam grup yang sudah dipisah akan dieksekusi secara independen, yang mungkin berarti mereka dieksekusi dalam urutan yang berbeda dari saat mereka dikelompokkan.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Expand an operation’s definition {#expand-an-operations-definition}"
msgstr "Perluas definisi operasi {#expand-an-operations-definition}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To view the operations that constitute a custom or predefined operation without ungrouping them, click **Expand definition** from the contextual menu to see the defining gates. Click the icon again to collapse the definition.\n"
msgstr "Untuk melihat operasi yang membentuk suatu operasi kustom atau predefined tanpa memisahkannya, klik **Expand definition** dari menu kontekstual untuk melihat Gate yang mendefinisikannya. Klik ikon tersebut lagi untuk menutup definisi.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Rename or delete a custom operation {#rename-or-delete-a-custom-operation}"
msgstr "Ganti nama atau hapus operasi kustom {#rename-or-delete-a-custom-operation}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To rename or delete a custom operation, right-click the operation in the operations catalog and select Rename or Delete. Deleting a custom operation from the operations catalog also deletes any instances of it on your circuit.\n"
msgstr "Untuk mengganti nama atau menghapus operasi kustom, klik kanan operasi di katalog operasi dan pilih Rename atau Delete. Menghapus operasi kustom dari katalog operasi juga akan menghapus semua instance-nya di Circuit-mu.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Deleting a custom operation from the circuit itself does not delete it from the operations catalog; you can only delete a custom operation from the catalog by using right-click and selecting Delete.\n"
msgstr "Menghapus operasi kustom dari Circuit itu sendiri tidak menghapusnya dari katalog operasi; kamu hanya bisa menghapus operasi kustom dari katalog dengan menggunakan klik kanan dan memilih Delete.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Add or remove registers {#add-or-remove-registers}"
msgstr "Tambah atau hapus register {#add-or-remove-registers}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To add or remove quantum or classical registers, click Edit → Manage registers. You can increase or decrease the number of qubits or bits in your circuit and rename the registers. Click **Ok** to apply the changes. You can also simply click the register name (e.g., `q[0]`) and use the options in the contextual menu to quickly add or delete registers or qubits.\n"
msgstr "Untuk menambah atau menghapus register kuantum atau klasik, klik Edit → Manage registers. Kamu bisa menambah atau mengurangi jumlah qubit atau bit di Circuit-mu serta mengganti nama register. Klik **Ok** untuk menerapkan perubahan. Kamu juga bisa langsung mengklik nama register (misal, `q[0]`) dan menggunakan opsi di menu kontekstual untuk dengan cepat menambah atau menghapus register atau qubit.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Add a conditional {#add-a-conditional}"
msgstr "Tambahkan kondisional {#add-a-conditional}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To add a conditional to a gate, drag the `if` operation to the gate and set the parameters in the Edit operation panel that automatically opens. You can also double-click a gate to access the Edit operation panel, and set the conditional parameters that way.\n"
msgstr "Untuk menambahkan kondisional ke Gate, seret operasi `if` ke Gate tersebut dan atur parameter di panel Edit operation yang otomatis terbuka. Kamu juga bisa klik dua kali Gate untuk mengakses panel Edit operation, dan mengatur parameter kondisional dengan cara tersebut.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Add a control modifier {#add-a-control-modifier}"
msgstr "Tambahkan control modifier {#add-a-control-modifier}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A control modifier yields a gate whose original operation is now contingent on the state of the control qubit. For more details, right-click the control modifier symbol in the operations catalog, then click Info.\n"
msgstr "Control modifier menghasilkan Gate yang operasi aslinya sekarang bergantung pada status qubit kontrol. Untuk detail lebih lanjut, klik kanan simbol control modifier di katalog operasi, lalu klik Info.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Drag the control modifier to a gate in order to add a control to it. A dot appears on the control qubit and a line connects it to the target qubit. To edit which qubit is the control or target, click the gate and select the Edit operation icon (or double-click the gate) to open the Edit operation panel, then specify your parameters. From the Edit operation panel, you can also remove a control from a qubit by clicking the x next to the qubit name.\n"
msgstr "Seret control modifier ke Gate untuk menambahkan kontrol padanya. Sebuah titik akan muncul di qubit kontrol dan garis menghubungkannya ke qubit target. Untuk mengedit qubit mana yang menjadi kontrol atau target, klik Gate dan pilih ikon Edit operation (atau klik dua kali Gate) untuk membuka panel Edit operation, lalu tentukan parametermu. Dari panel Edit operation, kamu juga bisa menghapus kontrol dari qubit dengan mengklik x di samping nama qubit.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Visualize with phase disks throughout your circuit {#visualize-with-phase-disks-throughout-your-circuit}"
msgstr "Visualisasikan dengan cakram fase di seluruh Circuit-mu {#visualize-with-phase-disks-throughout-your-circuit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To visualize the state of all qubits at any point in your circuit, drag the phase disk icon from the operations catalog and place it anywhere in your circuit. A column of barrier operations and a column of phase disks are added (one barrier operation and phase disk per qubit). Hover over each phase disk to read the state of the qubit at that point in the circuit. Note that adding the phase disks does not alter your circuit; they are merely a visualization tool.\n"
msgstr "Untuk memvisualisasikan status semua qubit di titik mana pun di Circuit-mu, seret ikon cakram fase dari katalog operasi dan tempatkan di mana saja di Circuit-mu. Sebuah kolom operasi barrier dan kolom cakram fase akan ditambahkan (satu operasi barrier dan cakram fase per qubit). Arahkan mouse ke setiap cakram fase untuk membaca status qubit di titik tersebut dalam Circuit. Perlu diperhatikan bahwa menambahkan cakram fase tidak mengubah Circuit-mu; itu hanyalah alat visualisasi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Read more about the [phase disk visualization](#phase-disk).\n"
msgstr "Baca lebih lanjut tentang visualisasi cakram fase [di sini.](#phase-disk)\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Export a circuit image {#export-a-circuit-image}"
msgstr "Ekspor gambar Circuit {#export-a-circuit-image}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To export an image of your circuit, select File → Export circuit image. The Export options window opens, where you can choose a theme (light, dark, white on black, or black on white), a format (.svg or .png), and whether you want to apply a line wrap. After you’ve chosen your options, click Export.\n"
msgstr "Untuk mengekspor gambar Circuit-mu, pilih File → Export circuit image. Jendela Export options akan terbuka, di mana kamu bisa memilih tema (terang, gelap, putih di atas hitam, atau hitam di atas putih), format (.svg atau .png), dan apakah ingin menerapkan line wrap. Setelah memilih opsi, klik Export.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Build your circuit with OpenQASM code {#3-build-your-circuit-with-openqasm-code}"
msgstr "3. Bangun Circuit-mu dengan kode OpenQASM {#3-build-your-circuit-with-openqasm-code}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"IBM Quantum Composer currently supports OpenQASM 2.0.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"IBM Quantum Composer saat ini mendukung OpenQASM 2.0.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "To open the code editor, click View → Panels → Code Editor.\n"
msgstr "Untuk membuka editor kode, klik View → Panels → Code Editor.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "See the [Composer operations glossary](#composer-operations-glossary) for OpenQASM references to gates and other operations.\n"
msgstr "Lihat [glosarium operasi Composer](#composer-operations-glossary) untuk referensi OpenQASM ke Gate dan operasi lainnya.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can define your own custom operations; see [Create a custom operation in OpenQASM](#create-a-custom-operation-in-openqasm).\n"
msgstr "Kamu bisa mendefinisikan operasi kustom sendiri; lihat [Buat operasi kustom di OpenQASM](#create-a-custom-operation-in-openqasm).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "For more information on using the OpenQASM language, including sample lines of code, see the [Introduction to OpenQASM](/guides/introduction-to-qasm) guide, or read the original research paper, [Open Quantum Assembly Language](https://arxiv.org/abs/1707.03429). The [table](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1707.03429.pdf#page=9) of OpenQASM language statements from the paper is reproduced below. The OpenQASM grammar can be found in [Appendix A](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1707.03429.pdf#page=21) of the paper.\n"
msgstr "Untuk informasi lebih lanjut tentang penggunaan bahasa OpenQASM, termasuk contoh baris kode, lihat panduan [Pengantar OpenQASM](/guides/introduction-to-qasm), atau baca makalah penelitian aslinya, [Open Quantum Assembly Language](https://arxiv.org/abs/1707.03429). [Tabel](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1707.03429.pdf#page=9) pernyataan bahasa OpenQASM dari makalah tersebut direproduksi di bawah ini. Tata bahasa OpenQASM dapat ditemukan di [Lampiran A](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1707.03429.pdf#page=21) dari makalah.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<p></p>\n"
"<table width=\"100%\">\n"
"<thead>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<th>Statement</th>\n"
"<th>Description</th>\n"
"<th>Example</th>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"</thead>\n"
"<tbody><tr>\n"
"<td><code>OPENQASM 2.0;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Denotes a file in OpenQASM format (see [a])</td>\n"
"<td><code>OPENQASM 2.0;</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>qreg name[size];</code></td>\n"
"<td>Declare a named register of qubits</td>\n"
"<td><code>qreg q[5];</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>creg name[size];</code></td>\n"
"<td>Declare a named register of bits</td>\n"
"<td><code>creg c[5];</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>include “filename”;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Open and parse another source file</td>\n"
"<td><code>include “qelib1.inc”;</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>gate name(params) qargs</code></td>\n"
"<td>Declare a unitary gate</td>\n"
"<td>(see text of paper)</td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>opaque name(params) qargs;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Declare an opaque gate</td>\n"
"<td>(see text of paper)</td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>// comment text</code></td>\n"
"<td>Comment a line of text</td>\n"
"<td><code>// oops!</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>U(theta,phi,lambda) qubit|qreg;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Apply built-in single-qubit gate(s) (see [b])</td>\n"
"<td><code>U(pi/2,2\\*pi/3,0) q[0];</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>CX qubit|qreg,qubit|qreg;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Apply built-in CNOT gate(s)</td>\n"
"<td><code>CX q[0],q[1];</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>measure qubit|qreg -&gt; bit|creg;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Make measurement(s) in $Z$ basis</td>\n"
"<td><code>measure q -&gt; c;</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>reset qubit|qreg;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Prepare qubit(s) in $\\vert 0\\rangle$</td>\n"
"<td><code>reset q[0];</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>gatename(params) qargs;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Apply a user-defined unitary gate</td>\n"
"<td><code>crz(pi/2) q[1],q[0];</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>if(creg==int) qop;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Conditionally apply quantum operation</td>\n"
"<td><code>if(c==5) CX q[0],q[1];</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>barrier qargs;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Prevent transformations across this source line</td>\n"
"<td><code>barrier q[0],q[1];</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"</tbody></table>\n"
msgstr ""
"<p></p>\n"
"<table width=\"100%\">\n"
"<thead>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<th>Pernyataan</th>\n"
"<th>Deskripsi</th>\n"
"<th>Contoh</th>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"</thead>\n"
"<tbody><tr>\n"
"<td><code>OPENQASM 2.0;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Menandai file dalam format OpenQASM (lihat [a])</td>\n"
"<td><code>OPENQASM 2.0;</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>qreg name[size];</code></td>\n"
"<td>Deklarasikan register qubit bernama</td>\n"
"<td><code>qreg q[5];</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>creg name[size];</code></td>\n"
"<td>Deklarasikan register bit bernama</td>\n"
"<td><code>creg c[5];</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>include \"filename\";</code></td>\n"
"<td>Buka dan parse file sumber lain</td>\n"
"<td><code>include \"qelib1.inc\";</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>gate name(params) qargs</code></td>\n"
"<td>Deklarasikan Gate unitary</td>\n"
"<td>(lihat teks makalah)</td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>opaque name(params) qargs;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Deklarasikan Gate opaque</td>\n"
"<td>(lihat teks makalah)</td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>// comment text</code></td>\n"
"<td>Komentari baris teks</td>\n"
"<td><code>// oops!</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>U(theta,phi,lambda) qubit|qreg;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Terapkan Gate single-Qubit bawaan (lihat [b])</td>\n"
"<td><code>U(pi/2,2\\*pi/3,0) q[0];</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>CX qubit|qreg,qubit|qreg;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Terapkan Gate CNOT bawaan</td>\n"
"<td><code>CX q[0],q[1];</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>measure qubit|qreg -&gt; bit|creg;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Lakukan pengukuran dalam basis $Z$</td>\n"
"<td><code>measure q -&gt; c;</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>reset qubit|qreg;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Siapkan qubit dalam status $\\vert 0\\rangle$</td>\n"
"<td><code>reset q[0];</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>gatename(params) qargs;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Terapkan Gate unitary yang didefinisikan pengguna</td>\n"
"<td><code>crz(pi/2) q[1],q[0];</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>if(creg==int) qop;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Terapkan operasi kuantum secara kondisional</td>\n"
"<td><code>if(c==5) CX q[0],q[1];</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>barrier qargs;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Cegah transformasi di seluruh baris sumber ini</td>\n"
"<td><code>barrier q[0],q[1];</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"</tbody></table>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\[a] This must appear as the first non-comment line of the file.\n"
msgstr "\\[a] Ini harus muncul sebagai baris non-komentar pertama dari file.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\[b] The parameters theta, phi, and lambda are given by *parameter expressions*; for more information, see [page 5 of the paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/1707.03429#page=5) and [Appendix A](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1707.03429.pdf#page=21).\n"
msgstr "\\[b] Parameter theta, phi, dan lambda diberikan oleh *ekspresi parameter*; untuk informasi lebih lanjut, lihat [halaman 5 dari makalah](https://arxiv.org/abs/1707.03429#page=5) dan [Lampiran A](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1707.03429.pdf#page=21).\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Create a custom operation in OpenQASM {#create-a-custom-operation-in-openqasm}"
msgstr "Buat operasi kustom di OpenQASM {#create-a-custom-operation-in-openqasm}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can define new unitary operations in the code editor (see the figure below for an example). The operations are applied using the statement `name(params) qargs;` just like the built-in operations. The parentheses are optional if there are no parameters.\n"
msgstr "Kamu bisa mendefinisikan operasi unitary baru di editor kode (lihat gambar di bawah untuk contohnya). Operasi diterapkan menggunakan pernyataan `name(params) qargs;` seperti operasi bawaan. Tanda kurung bersifat opsional jika tidak ada parameter.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To define a custom operation, enter it in the OpenQASM code editor using this format: `gatename(params) qargs;`. If you click **+Add** in the operations list, you will be prompted to enter a name for your custom operation, which you can then build in the code editor.\n"
msgstr "Untuk mendefinisikan operasi kustom, masukkan di editor kode OpenQASM menggunakan format ini: `gatename(params) qargs;`. Jika kamu mengklik **+Add** di daftar operasi, kamu akan diminta untuk memasukkan nama operasi kustom-mu, yang kemudian bisa kamu bangun di editor kode.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Once you have defined your custom operation, drag it onto the graphical editor and use the edit icon to fine-tune the parameters.\n"
msgstr "Setelah mendefinisikan operasi kustom, seret ke editor grafis dan gunakan ikon edit untuk menyesuaikan parameter.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Example of a custom operation | |\n"
"| --- | --- |\n"
"| The gates to be included in the custom operation: | ![Gates in the custom operation](/docs/images/guides/composer/763d3b42-4b6e-4409-817f-7d15abae2d76.avif)|\n"
"| The code for the new operation: | ![Customized new operation](/docs/images/guides/composer/db5856ca-751c-4f12-9f25-6060b9003687.avif) | \n"
"| The new operation in the graphical editor: | ![New operation](/docs/images/guides/composer/d7fb8ec5-5eae-4ad4-9972-1e3665b39b7f.avif) |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Contoh operasi kustom | |\n"
"| --- | --- |\n"
"| Gate yang akan disertakan dalam operasi kustom: | ![Gate dalam operasi kustom](/docs/images/guides/composer/763d3b42-4b6e-4409-817f-7d15abae2d76.avif)|\n"
"| Kode untuk operasi baru: | ![Operasi baru yang dikustomisasi](/docs/images/guides/composer/db5856ca-751c-4f12-9f25-6060b9003687.avif) |\n"
"| Operasi baru di editor grafis: | ![Operasi baru](/docs/images/guides/composer/d7fb8ec5-5eae-4ad4-9972-1e3665b39b7f.avif) |\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "4. Inspect your circuit, step-by-step {#4-inspect-your-circuit-step-by-step}"
msgstr "4. Periksa Circuit-mu, langkah demi langkah {#4-inspect-your-circuit-step-by-step}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Inspect mode de-mystifies the inner workings of the circuits you create. It steps through a simulation of your circuit, one layer at a time, so that you can see the state of the qubits as the computation evolves.\n"
msgstr "Mode inspeksi mengungkap cara kerja Circuit yang kamu buat. Mode ini melangkah melalui simulasi Circuit-mu, satu lapisan sekaligus, sehingga kamu bisa melihat status qubit saat komputasi berkembang.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the **View** menu, select the panels for the visualizations that you want to use.\n"
msgstr "Di menu **View**, pilih panel untuk visualisasi yang ingin kamu gunakan.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Click the **Inspect** toggle in the toolbar. Note that once Inspect mode is toggled on, you cannot add any more operations until it is turned off again.\n"
msgstr "Klik toggle **Inspect** di toolbar. Perlu diperhatikan bahwa setelah mode Inspect diaktifkan, kamu tidak bisa menambahkan operasi apa pun lagi sampai mode tersebut dinonaktifkan.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you built your circuit with the Freeform alignment turned on, note that Inspect mode automatically turns on the Left alignment.\n"
msgstr "Jika kamu membangun Circuit dengan perataan Freeform diaktifkan, perlu diperhatikan bahwa mode Inspect secara otomatis mengaktifkan perataan Left.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "To move step-by-step through visualizations of your circuit’s components, use the forward and rewind buttons.\n"
msgstr "Untuk melangkah maju mundur melalui visualisasi komponen Circuit-mu, gunakan tombol maju dan mundur.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Controls to step forward and backward, and to jump to a circuit's beginning or end.](/docs/images/guides/composer/5f2dfb7c-a244-405c-8950-f422a4408fcf.avif \"Inspect mode controls, in order: jump to the beginning of a circuit, step backward, play from one break point to the next, step forward, jump to the end of a circuit.\")\n"
msgstr "![Kontrol untuk melangkah maju dan mundur, serta untuk melompat ke awal atau akhir Circuit.](/docs/images/guides/composer/5f2dfb7c-a244-405c-8950-f422a4408fcf.avif \"Kontrol mode Inspect, secara berurutan: lompat ke awal Circuit, langkah mundur, putar dari satu break point ke berikutnya, langkah maju, lompat ke akhir Circuit.\")\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "To inspect only some operations, click the operations you want to be inspected, and a colored overlay appears over each that indicates they will be included when you run in Inspect mode. To unselect an operation, click on it again, and the overlay disappears.\n"
msgstr "Untuk memeriksa hanya beberapa operasi, klik operasi yang ingin diperiksa, dan overlay berwarna akan muncul di atasnya yang menandakan bahwa operasi tersebut akan disertakan saat kamu menjalankan mode Inspect. Untuk membatalkan pilihan operasi, klik lagi, dan overlay akan menghilang.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "To learn more about interpreting visualizations, see the [Visualizations](#visualizations) topic.\n"
msgstr "Untuk mempelajari lebih lanjut tentang interpretasi visualisasi, lihat topik [Visualisasi](#visualizations).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "To exit Inspect mode and return to editing your circuit, click the Inspect toggle in the toolbar.\n"
msgstr "Untuk keluar dari mode Inspect dan kembali mengedit Circuit-mu, klik toggle Inspect di toolbar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Randomness in the simulator\">\n"
"The simulator creates randomness by generating results based on a *seed*. The seed is the initial value introduced into the algorithm that generates pseudorandom numbers. You can see the seed number by selecting \"Visualizations seed\" from the Edit menu. You can also set the seed yourself by changing the value in the box.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Keacakan dalam simulator\">\n"
"Simulator menciptakan keacakan dengan menghasilkan hasil berdasarkan *seed*. Seed adalah nilai awal yang dimasukkan ke dalam algoritma yang menghasilkan bilangan pseudorandom. Kamu bisa melihat nomor seed dengan memilih \"Visualizations seed\" dari menu Edit. Kamu juga bisa mengatur seed sendiri dengan mengubah nilai di kotak tersebut.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run circuits and view results {#run-circuits-and-view-results}"
msgstr "Jalankan Circuit dan Lihat Hasil {#run-circuits-and-view-results}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Follow the steps below to run quantum circuits on QPUs and view the results.\n"
msgstr "Ikuti langkah-langkah berikut untuk menjalankan quantum circuit di QPU dan melihat hasilnya.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choose your job settings {#choose-your-job-settings}"
msgstr "Pilih pengaturan job {#choose-your-job-settings}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Click **Run circuit** in the upper right corner. In the window that opens, select an available QPU. You can also choose an instance, which is associated with a plan (such as the Open, Flex, or Premium Plans). The instance you choose affects which QPUs are available to you. Click the \"View details\" link in the table of QPUs to see more information on each QPU.\n"
msgstr "Klik **Run circuit** di pojok kanan atas. Di jendela yang terbuka, pilih QPU yang tersedia. Kamu juga bisa memilih instance, yang terkait dengan suatu plan (seperti Open, Flex, atau Premium Plan). Instance yang kamu pilih mempengaruhi QPU mana yang tersedia bagimu. Klik tautan \"View details\" di tabel QPU untuk melihat informasi lebih lanjut tentang masing-masing QPU.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, you can set the number of shots (executions) of your circuit that the backend will perform.\n"
msgstr "Selanjutnya, kamu bisa mengatur jumlah shot (eksekusi) dari circuit yang akan dilakukan Backend.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can optionally name the job and add tags in this panel as well. This will not change the name of the circuit. A pre-populated \"Composer\" tag makes it easier to filter your Workloads table by Composer jobs. You can remove this tag.\n"
msgstr "Kamu juga bisa secara opsional memberi nama job dan menambahkan tag di panel ini. Ini tidak akan mengubah nama circuit. Tag \"Composer\" yang sudah terisi sebelumnya memudahkan penyaringan tabel Workloads berdasarkan job Composer. Kamu bisa menghapus tag ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Window displaying job options.](/docs/images/guides/composer/composer-run.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Jendela yang menampilkan opsi job.](/docs/images/guides/composer/composer-run.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"When you run a circuit, it is automatically sent to the least-busy QPU, unless you specify a QPU in the Run settings. If you run the same circuit again, the QPU selection window will default to your previous choice.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Saat kamu menjalankan circuit, circuit tersebut secara otomatis dikirim ke QPU yang paling tidak sibuk, kecuali kamu menentukan QPU tertentu di pengaturan Run. Jika kamu menjalankan circuit yang sama lagi, jendela pemilihan QPU akan kembali ke pilihan sebelumnya secara default.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Click \"Run on (QPU name)\" {#click-run-on-qpu-name}"
msgstr "Klik \"Run on (nama QPU)\" {#click-run-on-qpu-name}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can view the job’s progress by clicking the \"View jobs\" button in the top-right corner, which will open the Workloads page in IBM Quantum Platform.\n"
msgstr "Kamu bisa melihat perkembangan job dengan mengklik tombol \"View jobs\" di pojok kanan atas, yang akan membuka halaman Workloads di IBM Quantum Platform.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "View results {#view-results}"
msgstr "Lihat hasil {#view-results}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Once your job completes, the details are updated in the Workloads table in IBM Quantum Platform.\n"
msgstr "Setelah job selesai, detailnya diperbarui di tabel Workloads di IBM Quantum Platform.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Jobs results page displays run details, diagrams of the original and the transpiled circuit, a histogram of the results, and OpenQASM and Qiskit tabs to view both original and transpiled circuits in OpenQASM or Qiskit.\n"
msgstr "Halaman Jobs results menampilkan detail eksekusi, diagram circuit asli dan circuit yang sudah di-transpile, histogram hasil, serta tab OpenQASM dan Qiskit untuk melihat circuit asli maupun yang sudah di-transpile dalam format OpenQASM atau Qiskit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can download the circuits and the histogram by clicking the menu in the upper right corner of each diagram, then selecting a format for the download (PNG, PDF, or SVG; additionally, you can export the histogram as a CSV file). You can open the OpenQASM circuits directly in Composer.\n"
msgstr "Kamu bisa mengunduh circuit dan histogram dengan mengklik menu di pojok kanan atas setiap diagram, lalu memilih format unduhan (PNG, PDF, atau SVG; selain itu, kamu bisa mengekspor histogram sebagai file CSV). Kamu bisa membuka circuit OpenQASM langsung di Composer.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Visualizations {#visualizations}"
msgstr "Visualisasi {#visualizations}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The live visualizations in IBM Quantum Composer show you different views of how quantum circuits affect the state of a collection of qubits. Each type of live visualization is explained in detail below.\n"
msgstr "Visualisasi langsung di IBM Quantum Composer menampilkan berbagai tampilan tentang bagaimana quantum circuit mempengaruhi keadaan sekumpulan qubit. Setiap jenis visualisasi langsung dijelaskan secara detail di bawah ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Randomness in the simulator\">\n"
"The live visualizations come from a single-shot statevector simulator, which is different from the QPU specified in the Run settings, which can have multiple shots. The simulator creates randomness by generating results based on a *seed*. The seed is the initial value introduced into the algorithm that generates pseudorandom numbers. You can see the seed number by selecting \"Visualizations seed\" from the Edit menu. You can also set the seed yourself by changing the value in the box.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Keacakan dalam simulator\">\n"
"Visualisasi langsung berasal dari simulator statevector satu shot, yang berbeda dari QPU yang ditentukan dalam pengaturan Run yang dapat memiliki banyak shot. Simulator menciptakan keacakan dengan menghasilkan hasil berdasarkan sebuah *seed*. Seed adalah nilai awal yang dimasukkan ke dalam algoritma yang menghasilkan angka pseudorandom. Kamu bisa melihat nomor seed dengan memilih \"Visualizations seed\" dari menu Edit. Kamu juga bisa mengatur seed sendiri dengan mengubah nilai di kotak tersebut.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "View visualizations {#view-visualizations}"
msgstr "Lihat visualisasi {#view-visualizations}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The live visualizations are shown in windows at the bottom of the Composer workspace (except the phase disk, which appears at the end of each qubit wire). You can choose any combination of statevector, probabilities, and q-sphere visualizations to appear at the bottom of the workspace. Select or unselect visualizations in the **View** menu.\n"
msgstr "Visualisasi langsung ditampilkan di jendela-jendela di bagian bawah workspace Composer (kecuali phase disk, yang muncul di ujung setiap wire qubit). Kamu bisa memilih kombinasi apa pun dari visualisasi statevector, probabilitas, dan q-sphere untuk ditampilkan di bagian bawah workspace. Pilih atau batalkan pilihan visualisasi di menu **View**.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Download visualizations {#download-visualizations}"
msgstr "Unduh visualisasi {#download-visualizations}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Download one of the visualizations at the bottom of the Composer workspace by clicking the \"More options\" menu in the visualization window. You can download visualizations as an SVG, a PNG, or a CSV of the underlying data. You can also download the visualization images of the measurement probabilities and statevector histograms as a PDF.\n"
msgstr "Unduh salah satu visualisasi di bagian bawah workspace Composer dengan mengklik menu \"More options\" di jendela visualisasi. Kamu bisa mengunduh visualisasi sebagai SVG, PNG, atau CSV dari data yang mendasarinya. Kamu juga bisa mengunduh gambar visualisasi dari histogram probabilitas pengukuran dan statevector sebagai PDF.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Phase disk {#phase-disk}"
msgstr "Phase disk {#phase-disk}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A single-qubit state can be represented as\n"
msgstr "Keadaan satu qubit dapat direpresentasikan sebagai\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{split}\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\sqrt{1-p}\\vert0\\rangle + e^{j\\varphi} \\sqrt{p} \\vert1\\rangle,\\end{split}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{split}\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\sqrt{1-p}\\vert0\\rangle + e^{j\\varphi} \\sqrt{p} \\vert1\\rangle,\\end{split}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $p$ is the probability that the qubit is in the $|1\\rangle$ state, and $\\varphi$ is the quantum phase. $p$ is strongly analogous to a classical probabilistic bit. For $p=0$, the qubit is in the $|0\\rangle$ state, for $p=1$ the qubit is in the $|1\\rangle$ state, and for $p=1/2$ the qubit is a 50/50 mixture. We call this a superposition as, unlike classical bits, this mixture can have a quantum phase. The phase disk visualizes this state.\n"
msgstr "di mana $p$ adalah probabilitas bahwa qubit berada dalam keadaan $|1\\rangle$, dan $\\varphi$ adalah phase kuantum. $p$ sangat mirip dengan bit probabilistik klasik. Untuk $p=0$, qubit berada dalam keadaan $|0\\rangle$, untuk $p=1$ qubit berada dalam keadaan $|1\\rangle$, dan untuk $p=1/2$ qubit adalah campuran 50/50. Kita menyebut ini sebagai superposisi karena, tidak seperti bit klasik, campuran ini dapat memiliki phase kuantum. Phase disk memvisualisasikan keadaan ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The phase disk at the terminus of each qubit in IBM Quantum Composer gives the local state of each qubit at the end of the computation. The components of the phase disk are described below.\n"
msgstr "Phase disk di ujung setiap qubit di IBM Quantum Composer memberikan keadaan lokal dari setiap qubit di akhir komputasi. Komponen-komponen phase disk dijelaskan di bawah ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Probability the qubit is in the** $|1\\rangle$ **state**\n"
msgstr "**Probabilitas qubit berada dalam keadaan** $|1\\rangle$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The probability that the qubit is in the $|1\\rangle$ state is represented by the blue disk fill.\n"
msgstr "Probabilitas bahwa qubit berada dalam keadaan $|1\\rangle$ direpresentasikan oleh isian disk berwarna biru.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![probability the qubit is in the 1 state](/docs/images/guides/composer/3e4140c6-9da0-46b0-85e4-a1509078d3e9.avif)\n"
msgstr "![probabilitas qubit berada dalam keadaan 1](/docs/images/guides/composer/3e4140c6-9da0-46b0-85e4-a1509078d3e9.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Quantum phase**\n"
msgstr "**Phase kuantum**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The quantum phase of the qubit state is given by the line that extends from the center of the diagram to the edge of the gray disk (which rotates counterclockwise around the center point).\n"
msgstr "Phase kuantum dari keadaan qubit diberikan oleh garis yang memanjang dari pusat diagram ke tepi disk abu-abu (yang berputar berlawanan arah jarum jam di sekitar titik pusat).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![phase of the local qubit state](/docs/images/guides/composer/7f047fde-c19e-46db-b596-be5da55e697e.avif)\n"
msgstr "![phase dari keadaan qubit lokal](/docs/images/guides/composer/7f047fde-c19e-46db-b596-be5da55e697e.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Example: phase disks for two different qubits**\n"
msgstr "**Contoh: phase disk untuk dua qubit berbeda**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![phase disk examples](/docs/images/guides/composer/0207fba8-8b4b-4611-9638-6cbe169e10c4.avif)\n"
msgstr "![contoh phase disk](/docs/images/guides/composer/0207fba8-8b4b-4611-9638-6cbe169e10c4.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two examples of the phase disk visualization. The first example is a $|1\\rangle$ state and the second shows the $(|0\\rangle-|1\\rangle)/\\sqrt{2}$ state with a nonzero relative phase.\n"
msgstr "Dua contoh visualisasi phase disk. Contoh pertama adalah keadaan $|1\\rangle$ dan yang kedua menunjukkan keadaan $(|0\\rangle-|1\\rangle)/\\sqrt{2}$ dengan phase relatif yang bukan nol.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Connection to the Bloch sphere**\n"
msgstr "**Hubungan dengan Bloch sphere**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The phase disk, which contains all the information in the Bloch sphere, is a two-dimensional representation of a qubit. To convert to the Bloch sphere representation: $x=2\\sqrt{p(1-p)}\\mathrm{Re}[e^{j\\varphi} ]$, $y=2\\sqrt{p(1-p)}\\mathrm{Im}[e^{j\\varphi} ]$, and $z=1-2p$.\n"
msgstr "Phase disk, yang memuat semua informasi dalam Bloch sphere, adalah representasi dua dimensi dari sebuah qubit. Untuk mengonversi ke representasi Bloch sphere: $x=2\\sqrt{p(1-p)}\\mathrm{Re}[e^{j\\varphi} ]$, $y=2\\sqrt{p(1-p)}\\mathrm{Im}[e^{j\\varphi} ]$, dan $z=1-2p$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**N-qubit states: maximum 15 qubits**\n"
msgstr "**Keadaan N-qubit: maksimum 15 qubit**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An N-qubit quantum state takes the form\n"
msgstr "Keadaan kuantum N-qubit berbentuk\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{split}\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\sqrt{1-p}\\vert0...0\\rangle + \\sum_{k=1}^{2^N-1}e^{j\\varphi_k} \\sqrt{p_k} \\vert k\\rangle,\\end{split}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{split}\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\sqrt{1-p}\\vert0...0\\rangle + \\sum_{k=1}^{2^N-1}e^{j\\varphi_k} \\sqrt{p_k} \\vert k\\rangle,\\end{split}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $p_k$ is the probability that the qubits are in the state $|k\\rangle$ with quantum phase $\\varphi_k$ with respect to the $|0...0\\rangle$ state. $p=\\sum_{k\\neq0}p_k$ is the probability that the qubits are not in the ground state $|0...0\\rangle$. Here it is simple to see that for an N-qubit quantum state there are $2^N-1$ probabilities and $2^N-1$ phases. The phase disk fails to represent this state, as N-qubit phase disks would only contain $N$ probabilities and $N$ phases; this is because most states are entangled and are not separable into independent single-qubit quantum states. To represent that full information is not contained in this visualization, we introduce the reduced purity as a component in the phase disk.\n"
msgstr "di mana $p_k$ adalah probabilitas bahwa qubit-qubit berada dalam keadaan $|k\\rangle$ dengan phase kuantum $\\varphi_k$ terhadap keadaan $|0...0\\rangle$. $p=\\sum_{k\\neq0}p_k$ adalah probabilitas bahwa qubit-qubit tidak berada dalam keadaan dasar $|0...0\\rangle$. Di sini mudah terlihat bahwa untuk keadaan kuantum N-qubit terdapat $2^N-1$ probabilitas dan $2^N-1$ phase. Phase disk gagal merepresentasikan keadaan ini, karena phase disk N-qubit hanya akan memuat $N$ probabilitas dan $N$ phase; hal ini karena sebagian besar keadaan saling terjerat (entangled) dan tidak dapat dipisahkan menjadi keadaan kuantum qubit tunggal yang independen. Untuk merepresentasikan bahwa informasi penuh tidak terkandung dalam visualisasi ini, kita memperkenalkan reduced purity sebagai komponen dalam phase disk.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Reduced purity of the qubit state**\n"
msgstr "**Reduced purity dari keadaan qubit**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The radius of the black ring on the phase disk represents the reduced purity of the qubit state, which for qubit $j$ in an $N$-qubit state $|\\psi\\rangle$ is given by $\\mathrm{Tr}\\left[\\mathrm{Tr}_{i\\neq j}[\\left|\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\right|\\right]^{2}]$. The reduced purity for a single qubit is in the range $[0.5, 1]$; a value of one indicates that the qubit is not entangled with any other party. In contrast, a reduced purity of $0.5$ shows that the qubit is left in the completely mixed state, and has some level of entanglement over the remaining $N-1$ qubits, and possibly even the environment.\n"
msgstr "Jari-jari cincin hitam pada phase disk merepresentasikan reduced purity dari keadaan qubit, yang untuk qubit $j$ dalam keadaan $N$-qubit $|\\psi\\rangle$ diberikan oleh $\\mathrm{Tr}\\left[\\mathrm{Tr}_{i\\neq j}[\\left|\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\right|\\right]^{2}]$. Reduced purity untuk satu qubit berada dalam rentang $[0.5, 1]$; nilai satu menunjukkan bahwa qubit tidak terjerat dengan pihak lain mana pun. Sebaliknya, reduced purity sebesar $0.5$ menunjukkan bahwa qubit berada dalam keadaan yang sepenuhnya tercampur, dan memiliki tingkat keterjeratan tertentu pada $N-1$ qubit yang tersisa, dan bahkan mungkin pada lingkungannya.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Probabilities view {#probabilities-view}"
msgstr "Tampilan Probabilities {#probabilities-view}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**8-qubit limit**\n"
msgstr "**Batas 8 qubit**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This view visualizes the probabilities of the quantum state as a bar graph. The horizontal axis labels the computational basis states. The vertical axis measures the probabilities in terms of percentages. In this view the quantum phases are not represented, and is therefore an incomplete representation. However, it is useful for predicting the outcomes if each qubit is measured and the value stored in its own classical bit.\n"
msgstr "Tampilan ini memvisualisasikan probabilitas dari keadaan kuantum sebagai diagram batang. Sumbu horizontal melabeli keadaan basis komputasi. Sumbu vertikal mengukur probabilitas dalam bentuk persentase. Dalam tampilan ini phase kuantum tidak direpresentasikan, sehingga merupakan representasi yang tidak lengkap. Namun, ini berguna untuk memprediksi hasil jika setiap qubit diukur dan nilainya disimpan dalam bit klasik masing-masing.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Consider the following quantum circuit and its probabilities view:\n"
msgstr "Perhatikan quantum circuit berikut dan tampilan probabilitasnya:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![a quantum circuit](/docs/images/guides/composer/2H-circuit.svg \"A circuit consisting of a column of Hadamards that creates an equal superposition of the computational basis states, followed by a two-qubit controlled-Z (CZ) gate.\")\n"
msgstr "![sebuah quantum circuit](/docs/images/guides/composer/2H-circuit.svg \"Circuit yang terdiri dari kolom Hadamard yang menciptakan superposisi merata dari keadaan basis komputasi, diikuti oleh Gate controlled-Z (CZ) dua qubit.\")\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Probabilities view of the previous circuit](/docs/images/guides/composer/probabilities.svg \"Probabilities view of the previous circuit.\")\n"
msgstr "![Tampilan Probabilities dari circuit sebelumnya](/docs/images/guides/composer/probabilities.svg \"Tampilan Probabilities dari circuit sebelumnya.\")\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The circuit puts the two qubits into the state $|\\psi\\rangle = (|00\\rangle + |01\\rangle+ |10\\rangle-|11\\rangle) / 2$. The computational basis states are $|00\\rangle, |10\\rangle, |01\\rangle$, and $|11\\rangle$. The probabilities for each of the computational states is 1/4.\n"
msgstr "Circuit menempatkan dua qubit ke dalam keadaan $|\\psi\\rangle = (|00\\rangle + |01\\rangle+ |10\\rangle-|11\\rangle) / 2.$ Keadaan basis komputasi adalah $|00\\rangle, |10\\rangle, |01\\rangle,$ dan $|11\\rangle.$ Probabilitas untuk masing-masing keadaan komputasi adalah 1/4.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Q-sphere view {#q-sphere-view}"
msgstr "Tampilan Q-sphere {#q-sphere-view}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**5-qubit limit**\n"
msgstr "**Batas 5 qubit**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The q-sphere represents the state of a system of one or more qubits by associating each computational basis state with a point on the surface of a sphere. A node is visible at each point. Each node’s radius is proportional to the probability ($p_k$) of its basis state, whereas the node color indicates the quantum phase ($\\varphi_k$).\n"
msgstr "Q-sphere merepresentasikan keadaan sistem satu atau lebih qubit dengan mengasosiasikan setiap keadaan basis komputasi dengan sebuah titik di permukaan bola. Sebuah node terlihat di setiap titik. Jari-jari setiap node sebanding dengan probabilitas ($p_k$) dari keadaan basisnya, sedangkan warna node menunjukkan phase kuantum ($\\varphi_k$).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The nodes are laid out on the q-sphere so that the basis state with all zeros (e.g., $|000\\rangle)$ is at its north pole, and the basis state with all ones (e.g., $|111\\rangle$) is at its south pole. Basis states with the same number of zeros (or ones) lie on a shared latitude of the q-sphere (e.g., $|001\\rangle, |010\\rangle, |100\\rangle$). Beginning at the north pole of the q-sphere and progressing southward, each successive latitude has basis states with a greater number of ones; the latitude of a basis state is determined by its [Hamming distance](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hamming_distance) from the zero state. The q-sphere contains complete information about the quantum state in a compact representation.\n"
msgstr "Node-node ditempatkan di q-sphere sehingga keadaan basis dengan semua nol (misalnya, $|000\\rangle)$ berada di kutub utaranya, dan keadaan basis dengan semua satu (misalnya, $|111\\rangle$) berada di kutub selatannya. Keadaan basis dengan jumlah nol (atau satu) yang sama berada pada lintang yang sama di q-sphere (misalnya, $|001\\rangle, |010\\rangle, |100\\rangle$). Mulai dari kutub utara q-sphere dan bergerak ke selatan, setiap lintang berikutnya memiliki keadaan basis dengan jumlah satu yang lebih banyak; lintang sebuah keadaan basis ditentukan oleh [jarak Hamming](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hamming_distance)-nya dari keadaan nol. Q-sphere memuat informasi lengkap tentang keadaan kuantum dalam representasi yang ringkas.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Consider the following quantum circuit and its q-sphere, which represent the state the circuit creates:\n"
msgstr "Perhatikan quantum circuit berikut dan q-sphere-nya, yang merepresentasikan keadaan yang diciptakan circuit tersebut:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![a quantum circuit](/docs/images/guides/composer/2H-circuit.svg)\n"
msgstr "![sebuah quantum circuit](/docs/images/guides/composer/2H-circuit.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![q-sphere view](/docs/images/guides/composer/q-sphere.avif)\n"
msgstr "![tampilan q-sphere](/docs/images/guides/composer/q-sphere.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can select, hold, and drag to rotate the q-sphere. To return the q-sphere to its default orientation, select the **rewind-arrow button** to the top right of the q-sphere.\n"
msgstr "Kamu bisa memilih, menahan, dan menyeret untuk memutar q-sphere. Untuk mengembalikan q-sphere ke orientasi defaultnya, pilih **tombol rewind-arrow** di pojok kanan atas q-sphere.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"What is the difference between a Bloch sphere and a q-sphere?\">\n"
"It is important to highlight that the q-sphere is **not** the same as the Bloch sphere, even for a single qubit. Indeed, like the [phase disk](#phase-disk), the Bloch sphere gives a *local* view of the quantum state, where each qubit is viewed on its own. When trying to understand how registers of qubits (multi-qubit states) behave upon the application of quantum circuits, it is more insightful to take a *global* view and look at the quantum state in its entirety. The q-sphere provides a visual representation of the quantum state, and thus this *global* viewpoint. Therefore, when exploring quantum applications and algorithms on small numbers of qubits, the q-sphere should be the primary visualization method.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Apa perbedaan antara Bloch sphere dan q-sphere?\">\n"
"Penting untuk digarisbawahi bahwa q-sphere **bukan** hal yang sama dengan Bloch sphere, bahkan untuk satu qubit sekalipun. Memang, seperti [phase disk](#phase-disk), Bloch sphere memberikan tampilan *lokal* dari keadaan kuantum, di mana setiap qubit dilihat secara tersendiri. Ketika mencoba memahami bagaimana register qubit (keadaan multi-qubit) berperilaku saat penerapan quantum circuit, lebih berwawasan untuk mengambil tampilan *global* dan melihat keadaan kuantum secara keseluruhan. Q-sphere menyediakan representasi visual dari keadaan kuantum, dan dengan demikian memberikan sudut pandang *global* ini. Oleh karena itu, ketika menjelajahi aplikasi dan algoritma kuantum pada jumlah qubit yang kecil, q-sphere seharusnya menjadi metode visualisasi utama.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Statevector view {#statevector-view}"
msgstr "Tampilan Statevector {#statevector-view}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**6-qubit limit**\n"
msgstr "**Batas 6 qubit**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It is common to call $\\sqrt{p_k}e^{i\\varphi_k}$ the quantum amplitude. This view visualizes the quantum amplitudes as a bar graph. The horizontal axis labels the computational basis states. The vertical axis measures the magnitude of the amplitudes ($\\sqrt{p_k}$) associated with each computational basis state. The color of each bar represents the quantum phase (${\\varphi_k}$).\n"
msgstr "Umum untuk menyebut $\\sqrt{p_k}e^{i\\varphi_k}$ sebagai amplitudo kuantum. Tampilan ini memvisualisasikan amplitudo kuantum sebagai diagram batang. Sumbu horizontal melabeli keadaan basis komputasi. Sumbu vertikal mengukur besarnya amplitudo ($\\sqrt{p_k}$) yang terkait dengan setiap keadaan basis komputasi. Warna setiap batang merepresentasikan phase kuantum (${\\varphi_k}$).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Consider the following quantum circuit and its statevector view:\n"
msgstr "Perhatikan quantum circuit berikut dan tampilan statevector-nya:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![statevector view](/docs/images/guides/composer/state-vector.svg \"The statevector at the terminus of the above circuit. The color wheel maps phase angle to color. The output state is expressed as a list of complex numbers.\")\n"
msgstr "![tampilan statevector](/docs/images/guides/composer/state-vector.svg \"Statevector di ujung circuit di atas. Roda warna memetakan sudut phase ke warna. Keadaan keluaran dinyatakan sebagai daftar bilangan kompleks.\")\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The circuit puts the two qubits into the state $|\\psi\\rangle = (|00\\rangle + |01\\rangle+ |10\\rangle-|11\\rangle) / 2$. The computational basis states are $|00\\rangle$, $|10\\rangle$, $|01\\rangle$, and $|11\\rangle$. The magnitudes of the amplitudes are $1/2$, and the quantum phases with respect to the ground state are $0$ for $|01\\rangle$ and $|10\\rangle$, and $\\pi$ for $|11\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr "Circuit menempatkan dua qubit ke dalam keadaan $|\\psi\\rangle = (|00\\rangle + |01\\rangle+ |10\\rangle-|11\\rangle) / 2$. Keadaan basis komputasi adalah $|00\\rangle$, $|10\\rangle$, $|01\\rangle$, dan $|11\\rangle$. Besarnya amplitudo adalah $1/2$, dan phase kuantum terhadap keadaan dasar adalah $0$ untuk $|01\\rangle$ dan $|10\\rangle$, serta $\\pi$ untuk $|11\\rangle$.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Composer operations glossary {#composer-operations-glossary}"
msgstr "Glosarium operasi Composer {#composer-operations-glossary}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This page is a reference that defines the various classical and quantum operations you can use to manipulate qubits in a quantum circuit. Quantum operations include quantum gates, such as the Hadamard gate, as well as operations that are not quantum gates, such as the measurement operation.\n"
msgstr "Halaman ini adalah referensi yang mendefinisikan berbagai operasi klasik dan kuantum yang bisa kamu gunakan untuk memanipulasi qubit dalam quantum circuit. Operasi kuantum mencakup quantum gate, seperti Hadamard gate, serta operasi yang bukan quantum gate, seperti operasi pengukuran.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each entry below provides details and the OpenQASM reference for each operation. See the topic on [Build your circuit with OpenQASM code](#3-build-your-circuit-with-openqasm-code) for more information.\n"
msgstr "Setiap entri di bawah ini memberikan detail dan referensi OpenQASM untuk setiap operasi. Lihat topik tentang [Bangun circuit dengan kode OpenQASM](#3-build-your-circuit-with-openqasm-code) untuk informasi lebih lanjut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The q-sphere image in each gate entry below shows the state after the gate operates on the initial equal superposition state $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^{n}}}\\sum_{i=0}^{2^{n}-1}|i\\rangle$, where $n$ is the number of qubits needed to support the gate. See the [q-sphere](#q-sphere-view) topic for more information on this visualization.\n"
msgstr "Gambar q-sphere di setiap entri gate di bawah ini menunjukkan keadaan setelah gate beroperasi pada keadaan superposisi merata awal $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^{n}}}\\sum_{i=0}^{2^{n}-1}|i\\rangle$, di mana $n$ adalah jumlah qubit yang diperlukan untuk mendukung gate tersebut. Lihat topik [q-sphere](#q-sphere-view) untuk informasi lebih lanjut tentang visualisasi ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can define a custom operation to use in IBM Quantum Composer. For instructions, see the [Create a custom operation in OpenQASM](#create-a-custom-operation-in-openqasm) topic.\n"
msgstr "Kamu bisa mendefinisikan operasi kustom untuk digunakan di IBM Quantum Composer. Untuk instruksinya, lihat topik [Buat operasi kustom dalam OpenQASM](#create-a-custom-operation-in-openqasm).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Gate colors\">\n"
"The gate colors are slightly different in the light and dark themes. The colors from the light theme are shown here.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Warna gate\">\n"
"Warna gate sedikit berbeda pada tema terang dan gelap. Warna dari tema terang ditampilkan di sini.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Click a quantum operation below to view its definition.\n"
msgstr "Klik operasi kuantum di bawah ini untuk melihat definisinya.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Classical gates {#classical-gates}"
msgstr "Gate klasik {#classical-gates}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**NOT Gate**\n"
msgstr "**Gate NOT**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The NOT gate, also known as the Pauli X gate, flips the $\\left|0\\right\\rangle$ state to $\\left|1\\right\\rangle$, and vice versa. The NOT gate is equivalent to RX for the angle $\\pi$ or to ‘HZH’.\n"
msgstr "Gate NOT, juga dikenal sebagai Gate Pauli X, membalik keadaan $\\left|0\\right\\rangle$ menjadi $\\left|1\\right\\rangle$, dan sebaliknya. Gate NOT setara dengan RX untuk sudut $\\pi$ atau dengan 'HZH'.\n"

